{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS4QoRwGfWmTaEKkTbPi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've added all 6 events from `docs/EVENTS.md`, sent through the existing `Analytics.capture` wrapper. `flutter analyze` reports no issues. Nothing was run on a device, there are no tests in the project, and I didn't check that events actually reach PostHog, since nothing could be sent to external services.\n\n**Registration screen** (`lib/screens/registration_screen.dart`):\n- `registration_email_started` and `registration_phone_started` fire once per screen opening, on the first character typed, not on every keystroke.\n- `loan_amount_changed` fires when the user lets go of the slider (`onChangeEnd`), with `amount`. That's one event per drag, not one per slider step.\n- `terms_accepted` fires only when the checkbox is ticked, not when it's cleared.\n- `registration_continue_tapped` sends `amount` and `terms`, then opens the offers screen.\n- Email and phone number are not sent anywhere; only the fact that typing started is reported.\n\n**Offers screen** (`lib/screens/offer_screen.dart`):\n- `offers_scrolled` fires when a scroll stops, and only if the user has scrolled further down than before. So `offset` shows how far they got, and scrolling up and down doesn't create duplicates.\n- To support this, `OfferScreen` is now a `StatefulWidget`.\n\nI avoided firing events on every change because you're on the PostHog free tier. Per-keystroke and per-pixel events would quickly use up the quota and clutter the funnels.\n\n**Open questions for product** (also in ANSWER.md):\n- `offset` is in screen pixels, so it varies with screen size and isn't comparable across devices.\n- `terms_accepted` will fire again if the user unticks and re-ticks the box.\n- `terms` in `registration_continue_tapped` will always be `true`, because Continue is disabled until terms are accepted.\n\nWhen I ran `flutter analyze`, the Flutter tooling modified `analysis_options.yaml` on its own and `pub get` created `pubspec.lock` and `.dart_tool`. I reverted the file and deleted those, so the only changes left are the two screen files and the new `ANSWER.md`. Nothing is committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":273,"cache_read_input_tokens":29812,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":273},"output_tokens":713,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f12e137e-c150-4e06-9169-eb5362503ed1","uuid":"2c1514b1-5fb5-4cd5-a15c-e695ec74d765","timestamp":"2026-10-27T03:49:33.975Z","request_id":"req_011CgS4QoBKAgQnmH19UzFNx"}
